  data: {
    LLM: "Save your high cards (Aces/Kings) for consecutive plays. Winning one Ace is useless if you lose the next trick. You need Ace THEN King to secure the pile.\n\nThe 'Break' Strategy: If the opponents have a huge heap building up, throw your highest card to win ONE trick just to break their streak, even if you can't win the second one. This keeps the heap in limbo.\n\nSignaling: Discarding a specific low card to tell your partner 'I have the master of this suit, let me win the next one'. In 'No Trump' variants, leading a suit often calls for a trump based on suit preference.",
